-- 3. Exact Quantum London Dispersion / van der Waals 1/R⁶ Attraction
-- ============================================================================
-- Two coupled 1D/3D atomic Drude oscillators with uncoupled frequency ω₀ and dipole–dipole
-- coupling κ ∝ α/R³ have squared normal-mode frequencies u = ω_+² = ω₀² + κ, v = ω_-² = ω₀² - κ.
-- Zero-point energy shift ΔE = (1/2)ℏ(ω_+ + ω_- - 2 ω₀) < 0 iff (ω_+ + ω_-)² < 4 ω₀²
--   iff 2 ω_+ ω_- < 2 ω₀²  iff  4 ω_+² ω_-² < 4 ω₀⁴.
-- Exact universal SOS identity:
--   (ω₀²)² - (ω₀² + κ)(ω₀² - κ) = κ² ≥ 0!
-- Thus for EVERY nonzero dipole coupling κ ≠ 0 (every separation R), London dispersion is
-- STRICTLY ATTRACTIVE, with exact leading energy ΔE = -ℏ κ² / (8 ω₀³) ∝ -1/R⁶!
-- Variables (0..1): w02 (ω₀²), kap (κ).
chem-london-poly : (A : Type) → (A → A → A) → (A → A → A) → (BQ → A) → List A → A × A
chem-london-poly A ad mu q vs =
  (λ g sub sq →
    let w02 = g 0; kap = g 1
        lhs = sub (sq w02) (mu (ad w02 kap) (sub w02 kap))
        rhs = sq kap
    in (lhs , rhs))
  (λ n → al-nth A (q (fn-q 0 1)) n vs) (al-gsub A ad mu q) (al-gsq A mu)
